---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// ─── EDIT THESE THREE, THEN REDEPLOY ─────────────────────────────────
// 1. Public PanelPicker URL (the page people vote on). Until set, the
//    vote button renders as "link coming" instead of a broken link.
const PANELPICKER_URL = "https://participate.sxsw.com/flow/sxsw/sxsw27/community-voting-sxsw/page/community-voting/session/1785011734260001qe1c";
// 2. The keystone clip. Paste a YouTube/Vimeo EMBED url (…/embed/ID) or a
//    direct .mp4 url. Until set, a tasteful "recording in progress" slot shows.
const CLIP_URL = "";
const CLIP_IS_MP4 = false; // true if CLIP_URL is a direct .mp4 file
// 3. Free tracking pixels (optional). Paste the numeric IDs only; empty = off.
const META_PIXEL_ID = "";        // Meta/Facebook Pixel ID
const LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID = "";  // LinkedIn Insight Tag partner ID
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

const hasVote = PANELPICKER_URL.trim().length > 0;
const hasClip = CLIP_URL.trim().length > 0;
---
<Base
  title="Who Sings the 'We'? — Vault Human at SXSW 2027"
  description="A PanelPicker proposal for SXSW 2027 — community voting closed Aug 23; results come later this fall. Who sings the “we” when you've been optimized out of your own world? Read the idea, and leave a comment if it speaks to you."
 image="https://www.vaulthuman.com/og-sxsw.png">
{META_PIXEL_ID && (
  <script type="text/javascript" set:html={`
    !function(f,b,e,v,n,t,s){if(f.fbq)return;n=f.fbq=function(){n.callMethod?n.callMethod.apply(n,arguments):n.queue.push(arguments)};if(!f._fbq)f._fbq=n;n.push=n;n.loaded=!0;n.version='2.0';n.queue=[];t=b.createElement(e);t.async=!0;t.src=v;s=b.getElementsByTagName(e)[0];s.parentNode.insertBefore(t,s)}(window,document,'script','https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js');
    fbq('init','${META_PIXEL_ID}');fbq('track','PageView');
  `} />
)}
{LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID && (
  <script type="text/javascript" set:html={`
    _linkedin_partner_id="${LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID}";window._linkedin_data_partner_ids=window._linkedin_data_partner_ids||[];window._linkedin_data_partner_ids.push(_linkedin_partner_id);
    (function(l){if(!l){window.lintrk=function(a,b){window.lintrk.q.push([a,b])};window.lintrk.q=[]}var s=document.getElementsByTagName("script")[0];var b=document.createElement("script");b.type="text/javascript";b.async=true;b.src="https://snap.licdn.com/li.lms-analytics/insight.min.js";s.parentNode.insertBefore(b,s)})(window.lintrk);
  `} />
)}

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="pagehead">
    <p class="eyebrow">SXSW 2027 &middot; Community voting closed</p>
    <h1>Who Sings the &ldquo;We&rdquo;?</h1>
    <p class="dek">Optimized out of your own world &mdash; one flawless assist at a time. This is a SXSW 2027 PanelPicker proposal &mdash; <strong>community voting closed Aug 23; results come from SXSW later this fall.</strong> Read the idea below, and if it speaks to your own work, leave a comment on the proposal.</p>
  </div>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- Keystone clip slot -->
  {hasClip && (
  <section class="speaking">
    <h2 class="sec">The idea, in ninety seconds</h2>
    {hasClip ? (
      CLIP_IS_MP4 ? (
        <video controls preload="metadata" style="width:100%;max-width:720px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;display:block;margin:8px auto 0">
          <source src={CLIP_URL} type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      ) : (
        <div style="position:relative;width:100%;max-width:720px;margin:8px auto 0;aspect-ratio:16/9;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden">
          <iframe src={CLIP_URL} title="Who Sings the We — 90 second clip" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0"></iframe>
        </div>
      )
    ) : null}
  </section>
  )}

  <hr class="rule" />

  <section class="speaking">
    <h2 class="sec">The proposal</h2>
    <p class="talk-meta">SXSW 2027 PanelPicker proposal &middot; community voting closed Aug 23 &middot; Austin &middot; Tech &amp; AI</p>
    <p class="talk-title">Who Sings the &ldquo;We&rdquo;? Optimized Out of Your Own World</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>In 1985, forty-six of the biggest voices on earth walked into one studio to record &ldquo;We Are the World.&rdquo; Quincy Jones taped a sign on the door: <em>check your ego at the door.</em> For one night the stars stopped being stars and became a chorus &mdash; imperfect, breathing, handing the melody to each other. The thing that made it beautiful was the seam between voices. The &ldquo;we.&rdquo;</p>
      <p>Now put today&rsquo;s AI in that studio. Every note is flawless. And something you can&rsquo;t name at first is missing &mdash; and then you can. There&rsquo;s no seam. There&rsquo;s no &ldquo;we.&rdquo;</p>
      <p>I&rsquo;m not afraid of AI being wrong. I use it every day and I want it to get better. What I keep watching is what happens when it&rsquo;s <strong>right</strong> &mdash; so right, so often, that the decision quietly stops being ours. No one takes it. We hand it over, one excellent answer at a time, until a life is full of choices that were all correct and none of them ours. The law has had a name for that for four hundred years: <em>undue influence</em>. This is the perfected version &mdash; no villain, no harm, no alarm.</p>
      <p>This talk is about staying the one who sings. What a room will actually do together:</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="steps" style="margin-top:8px">
      <li><strong>Whose decision was that, really?</strong> Run a 400-year-old legal test on the last thing you asked an AI to help you decide.</li>
      <li><strong>No one is pressuring you.</strong> The answer is just so good that agreeing feels like thinking. Learn to notice the moment you stopped choosing.</li>
      <li><strong>Delegate the task, never the judgment.</strong> A simple rule for what AI can carry and what a human has to hold &mdash; the values, the people, the direction.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:18px">
      <p>Underneath it is the mirror: artificial intelligence on one side, authentic intelligence &mdash; human, lived, accountable &mdash; on the other. As one gets sharper, the other has to get wiser. More discerning, more empathetic, more able to say <em>this one&rsquo;s mine.</em> That&rsquo;s the work. That&rsquo;s what I want an Austin room to do together.</p>
      <p><strong>Let the machine be brilliant. Let us get wise. And keep singing the part only a &ldquo;we&rdquo; can sing.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- Vote CTA — never gated behind a form -->
  <section class="speaking" style="text-align:center">
    <h2 class="sec">Add your voice</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="max-width:620px;margin:0 auto 6px">Community voting closed <strong>Sunday, August 23</strong> &mdash; results come from SXSW later this fall. The proposal page stays open: a specific, personal comment is still read, and still counts.</p>
    {hasVote ? (
      <div class="ctarow" style="margin-top:22px">
        <a class="btn-fill" href={PANELPICKER_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the proposal &amp; leave a comment &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    ) : (
      <div class="ctarow" style="margin-top:22px">
        <span class="btn-line" style="opacity:.55;cursor:default">Proposal link goes live once the public PanelPicker URL is confirmed</span>
      </div>
    )}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:14px">No account or email is required to read the idea. Nothing here is gated behind a form.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- Optional opt-in — clearly secondary -->
  <section class="speaking" style="text-align:center">
    <h2 class="sec">Want the field note?</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="max-width:600px;margin:0 auto 4px">Optional: if the idea touched something in your own work, we&rsquo;ll send you the one-page <em>Whole-First</em> field note &mdash; the three questions, and the Silent Deferral map. No pitch, one relationship.</p>
    <div class="cta" style="margin-top:20px"><a class="btn-line" href="#" data-open-form>Send me the Whole-First field note</a></div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
